From: brcmfmac GTK rekey experiments <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wifi: brcmfmac: scope GTK replay recovery to BCM43430/2

Firmware 9.88.4.77 (FWID 01-3b307371) can reject a changed CCMP GTK with
BCME_REPLAY when replacing an occupied group-key slot. A bounded five-
rotation test recovered two such failures by clearing the selected slot
and retrying the unchanged key and receive sequence once.

Restrict this recovery to that chip revision and firmware build in
station mode. Exclude pairwise and extended keys, missing/invalid
receive sequences, non-CCMP keys, and keys matching any cached CCMP key.
Preserve the original firmware status per operation under the existing
firmware-interface lock; do not infer BCME_REPLAY from EBADE or toggle
shared error-reporting state. Transport failures and other firmware
errors must not trigger recovery.

This is a scoped workaround, not a general firmware fix. The host cache
cannot establish the firmware's full replay state; over-the-air replay
resistance remains a separate validation requirement.

---

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
index c493f29..4f3c14d 100644
